Now clear. NODE action transition must be one of:
- {type:"DISSOLVE"|"SMART_ANIMATE"|"SCROLL_ANIMATE", easing, duration}
- {type:"MOVE_IN"|"MOVE_OUT"|"PUSH"|"SLIDE_IN"|"SLIDE_OUT", direction, matchLayers, easing, duration}

For app-like navigation, DISSOLVE with short duration or SMART_ANIMATE. Use {type:"SMART_ANIMATE",duration:0.3,easing:{type:"EASE_OUT"}}? Easing format: {type:"EASE_OUT"} valid (Easing enum: LINEAR | EASE_IN | EASE_OUT | EASE_IN_OUT | EASE_IN_BACK etc. or {type:"CUSTOM_BEZIER"...}). Use easing:{type:"EASE_OUT"}, duration:0.3.

For overlay-ish screens (07/09/10/12) a SLIDE_IN bottom would be nice but direction+matchLayers required; keep it simple: SMART_ANIMATE for all, or DISSOLVE. Use SMART_ANIMATE duration 0.3 EASE_OUT — matches mobile feel and is safe between frames with matching layers.

Test then apply all 30 wires.

